error[ffi_parameter_type]: `x` of `fill_wide` is declared `i32`, and the header's `long long *` points at a different width or sign — clang read the header, and C writes back exactly the bytes the header expects
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-559-a-wider-pointee-is-refused-at-build-not-at-run.hero:15:25
     |
  15 |     function fill_wide(@x: i32)  #~ ffi_parameter_type
     |                         ^
  note: §4.19: a C out-parameter is an `@` parameter, and what it points at is held to the header's own width and sign — `u64` where it says `size_t *`, `i32` where it says `int *`
  fix (guess): declare `x` as `@x: i64`
